A||||3||Jimmy||Tightening Rockers on new Small Block||||5||
Z||000000||Jimmy||04-27-2001||12:11 AM||||First off the engine(0 miles full rebuild) has the following: hydraulic lifters, Z28 springs, and a cam thats more than stock but nothing wild.<BR>  <BR>I'm not sure if I adjusted the rockers right but here is what I did.<P>1.Turned the engine over until I got TDC on cylinder #1<BR>2.Tightened both the intake and exhaust rockers down until I couldn't spin the pushrods between my fingers.<BR>3.From the point where I couldn't spin the pushrods with my fingers, I gave the nut an extra 1/2 turn.<BR>4.Repeated the above steps with the rest of the cylinders, 1,8,4,3,6,5,7,2.<P>Seems like every other website said something a little different.  These were the steps that were repeated the most.<P>TIA<P>Jim||||reg||5
Z||000001||hugh||04-27-2001||07:05 AM||||It sounds like you may have made them too tight.You should spin the pushrods till you feel drag on them(0 clearance),then you want some preload.Some people go 1/4 turn,some go 1/2 turn.It's not critical. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Archie||04-27-2001||08:21 AM||||I agree sounds like you got them too tight. We really need more info about the engine.<P>Is it a roller cam? Roller rockers? Is the cam new? Did the cam come with a cam card that tells you where to adjust the lash?<P>If the lash is supposed to be set at "0" then you have tightened them down too far.<P>On a flat tappet cam with stamped rockers, I adjust them like Hugh says with 1/4 turn.<P>Archie<p>[This message has been edited by Archie (edited 04-27-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||Jimmy||04-28-2001||02:40 AM||||Guys its a flat tappet, no rollers.  They are the stock stamped rockers.  New cam, don't have cam card.  I know the cam isn't much different then what people call an "RV" or tourqe cam.<P>I went back and followed my original procedure but did just about a 1/4 turn instead of a half.  <P>I have seen and heard from many people that if you tighten the rockers down(Hydraulic lifters, stock rockers, not to aggresive cam) to the point where you can't spin the pushrods you can just leave it at that also.<P>Thanks again for any advice or help.<P>Jim||||reg||1
